{
  "id": "course-enrolment",
  "name": "Course Enrolment",
  "difficulty": "hl",
  "summary": "A higher-level dataset for grouped calculations, joins, averages, and HAVING clauses.",
  "focus": ["JOIN", "GROUP BY", "HAVING", "AVG"],
  "relationshipHighlights": ["One-to-many", "Many-to-many", "Composite key"],
  "defaultQuery": "SELECT d.DepartmentName, COUNT(*) AS EnrolledCount, ROUND(AVG(e.Score), 1) AS AverageScore FROM ENROLLMENT e JOIN COURSE c ON e.CourseID = c.CourseID JOIN DEPARTMENT d ON c.DepartmentID = d.DepartmentID GROUP BY d.DepartmentName HAVING COUNT(*) >= 3 ORDER BY AverageScore DESC;",
  "notes": [
    "ENROLLMENT is a junction table with a composite key made from StudentID and CourseID.",
    "Grouped queries can summarise how many students each department has and what their average score is."
  ],
  "tables": [
    {
      "name": "DEPARTMENT",
      "description": "Departments that own courses.",
      "kind": "entity",
      "diagram": { "x": 24, "y": 46 },
      "columns": [
        { "name": "DepartmentID", "type": "TEXT", "notNull": true },
        { "name": "DepartmentName", "type": "TEXT", "notNull": true },
        { "name": "Office", "type": "TEXT", "notNull": true }
      ],
      "primaryKey": ["DepartmentID"],
